I've updated my shallow water patch (new URL:
http://www.greyfire.org/~l/terrain.diff)

I've added a new terrain type: marble columns
* White '|'s
* Treated as barriers.
* Can be mined, chewed or stone-to-fleshed.
* If you destroy one, there is a good chance that you'll send the
ceiling crashing around your ears (scroll of earth effect, centered on
the column).

The draw is that they appear in standard dungeon rooms, altering their
topology somewhat. Maybe they could be utilised during combat?

Also, puddles of shallow water can now randomly appear in standard
dungeon rooms! If the puddle is significantly large, piranhas may be
generated in it as well.



